The relation list (*) is not a complete presentation of the category of nonempty finite sets. Missing are, for example:
  - relations between consecutive degeneracies, such as k_n k_{n+1} being invariant under all permutations of {n,n+1,n+2};
  - interaction between k_{n+1} and permutations moving n or n+1 beyond σ_{n+1};
  - relations among ∂'s and k's of different levels.
This matters only if Grothendieck intended a full presentation.
